The '''Nimbanels''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[Reptile|reptilian]] [[species]] that were [[Homeworld|native]] to [[Nimban]]. They could be found demonstrating their talents throughout the galaxy, particularly in business and government. They were also famed for problem-solving skills.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> [[Jay Igno]] was a Nimbanel [[air taxi]] [[Pilot|driver]] on [[Coruscant]].<ref name="Jay Igno" /> Five [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]], a [[Unidentified Nimbanel bounty hunter|Nimbanel]] [[bounty hunter]] and his [[Ranat]] [[Unidentified Ranat bounty hunter|colleague]] attempted to apprehend the [[Trandoshan]] bounty hunter [[Bossk'wassak'Cradossk|Bossk]] but were instead knocked unconscious.<ref name="EG">''[[Ezra's Gamble]]''</ref> 

{{Species-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The illustration of a Nimbanel by [[Tim McDonagh]] that was included in the [[2018]] book ''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]'' was based on<ref name="Alien Archive" /> a drawing of [[Rohlan Dyre]] by<ref name="TolibaoDeviantArt">{{DeviantArt|username=harveytolibao|url=harveytolibao/art/Mandalorian-50878174|name=[[Harvey Tolibao]]|text=Mandalorian|date=2007-03-15}}</ref> the ''[[Star Wars]]'' illustrator [[Harvey Tolibao]].<ref name="KOTOR12">[[Knights of the Old Republic 12|''Knights of the Old Republic'' 12]]</ref> Nimbanel were brought back into live action for the first time since [[Star Wars: Episode VI Return of the Jedi]] in [[Star Wars: The Book of Boba Fett]]'s episode [[Chapter 4: The Gathering Storm]] via a copy of the mold made for [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope]]<ref name="Tom Spina Nimbanel BOBF E-Mail">{{EmailCite|email=File:TomSpinaEmailNimbanelBOBF.png|creator=Tom Spina|date=2025-10-28}}</ref>

